   "baseline": "Processor only, start to finish",
   "note": "Each bar is the time to produce one full hedging ladder. The first two are the same job done two ways, start to finish, and they land in much the same place. The bottom two break the second one open: almost all of it is rebuilding the curve, once for every quoted price moved, and only the small remainder is valuing the trades. Rebuilding runs on the processor and takes the same time either way, which is why the GPU makes almost no difference. Faster hardware is not the answer here; doing fewer rebuilds is.",
